":"M","key":"søgaardmettepau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"5ce4f246-03bc-4e72-b36a-eb5f76e5e5cb","name":"Søgaard, Mette","name_org":"Søgaard, M","orcid":"0000-0002-2830-4968","rank":71,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"21","corresponding":null,"first":"S","key":"szmitspau","last":"Szmit","name":"Szmit, S","rank":72,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"S","key":"trompetspau","last":"Trompet","name":"Trompet, S","rank":73,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"P","key":"vassalppau","last":"Vassal","name":"Vassal, P","rank":74,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"16","corresponding":null,"first":"C","key":"vissercpau","last":"Visser","name":"Visser, C","rank":75,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"22","corresponding":null,"first":"L M","key":"vanvlietlmpau","last":"van Vliet","name":"van Vliet, L M","rank":76,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"17","corresponding":null,"first":"E","key":"wilsonepau","last":"Wilson","name":"Wilson, E","rank":77,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"F A","key":"klokfapau","last":"Klok","name":"Klok, F A","rank":78,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"S I R","key":"noblesirpau","last":"Noble","name":"Noble, S I R","rank":79,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37276718"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.thromres.2023.05.008","issn":["00493848","08960569"],"issn_org":["00493848"],"journal":"Thrombosis Research","pages":"54-60","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Thrombosis Research","volume":"228"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85164232931"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8d8a07e4-b784-4ce2-a011-ca202b9ffae6"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Towards optimal use of antithrombotic therapy of people with cancer at the end of life : A research protocol for the development and implementation of the SERENITY shared decision support tool","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-673868","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Fungi often adapt to environmental stress by altering their size, shape, or rate of cell division. These morphological changes require reorganization of the cell wall, a structural feature external to the cell membrane composed of highly interconnected polysaccharides and glycoproteins. Lytic polysaccharide monooxygenases (LPMOs) are copper-dependent enzymes that are typically secreted into the extracellular space to catalyze initial oxidative steps in the degradation of complex biopolymers such as chitin and cellulose. However, their roles in modifying endogenous microbial carbohydrates are poorly characterized. The CEL1 gene in the human fungal pathogen Cryptococcus neoformans (Cn) is predicted by sequence homology to encode an LPMO of the AA9 enzyme family. The CEL1 gene is induced by host physiological pH and temperature, and it is primarily localized to the fungal cell wall. Targeted mutation of the CEL1 gene revealed that it is required for the expression of stress response phenotypes, including thermotolerance, cell wall integrity, and efficient cell cycle progression. Accordingly, a cel1 Delta deletion mutant was avirulent in two models of C. neoformans infection. Therefore, in contrast to LPMO activity in other microorganisms that primarily targets exogenous polysaccharides, these data suggest that CnCel1 promotes intrinsic fungal cell wall remodeling events required for efficient adaptation to the host environment. Author summaryFungi need to adapt quickly to environmental stresses to thrive. The fungal cell wall, which supplies support and integrity to the cell, is an essential compartment to react and interact with the surrounding environment. Rapid changes within the carbohydrate composition and architecture occur in response to environmental stresses. Lytic polysaccharide monooxygenases (LPMOs) are mononuclear copper-enzymes, secreted by microbes to assist in the first steps of remodeling and degradation of complex and recalcitrant carbohydrates. In this study we explore the role of the putative AA9 family LPMO CnCel1 for growth and virulence of the fungal human pathogen Cryptococcus neoformans. The CEL1 gene is highly up-regulated in presence of host stresses and a cel1 Delta mutant strain is avirulent in a murine model of infection. Downstream analysis of virulence-associated phenotypes identified the CEL1 gene to be required for thermotolerance as well as cell wall integrity, and efficient cell cycle progression in presence of host-mimicking stresses. Based upon those findings, we propose that CnCel1 likely promotes intrinsic fungal cell wall remodeling events essential for adaptation to the host environment.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Probst, Corinna","Hallas-Møller, Magnus","Ipsen, Johan Ø.","Brooks, Jacob S.","Andersen, Karsten","Haon, Mireille","Berrin, Jean-Guy","Martens, Helle Juel","Nichols, Connie A.","Johansen, Katja S.","Alspaugh, J. Andrew"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-671000"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France","United States"],"glorg":["Aix-Marseille University","All Global Affiliations","Duke University","University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill"],"keyword":["Adaptation","Capsule","Cellulose","Degradation","GENE","Hydrolysis","Insights","Lignocellulose","Proteins","SYSTEM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a fungal lytic polysaccharide monooxygenase is required for cell wall integrity thermotolerance and virulence of the fungal human pathogen i cryptococcus neoformans i","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.ppat.1010946","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-671000","identifier":[{"id":"85159553278","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10166503","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37099613","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000975683700002","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-d1846565-5596-4085-b0af-b4f4c0c588d8"],"keyword":["ADAPTATION","CAPSULE","CELLULOSE","DEGRADATION","GENE","HYDROLYSIS","INSIGHTS","LIGNOCELLULOSE","PROTEINS","SYSTEM"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C0F2004D9C8C0CEAE0A86211CCBBC3B7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.ppat.1010946","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/346599975/A_fungal_lytic_polysaccharide_monooxygenase_is_required_for_cell_wall_integrity.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"duke university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Duke University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Forest and Bioressources"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of north carolina at chapel hill","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fr","key":"aix marseille university","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Aix-Marseille University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Corinna","key":"probstpau","last":"Probst","name":"Probst, Corinna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Magnus J.","key":"hallasmollerpau","last":"Hallas-Moller","locid":"e787ea5d-609f-4779-8cb9-0100bac39c15","name":"Hallas-Møller, Magnus","name_org":"Hallas-Moller, Magnus J.","orcid":"0000-0002-0900-2315","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Johan Ø.","key":"ipsenpau","last":"Ipsen","locid":"e0de582a-8537-48a7-a725-d55f112d959e","name":"Ipsen, Johan Ø.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jacob S.","key":"brookspau","last":"Brooks","name":"Brooks, Jacob S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Karsten","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"f36e3311-a0a1-41d2-b360-1dd360e4d529","name":"Andersen, Karsten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Mireille","key":"haonpau","last":"Haon","name":"Haon, Mireille","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Jean-Guy","key":"berrinpau","last":"Berrin","name":"Berrin, Jean-Guy","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Helle","key":"martenspau","last":"Martens","locid":"cd7f808e-0b4a-4423-9846-d3a81d0fad26","name":"Martens, Helle Juel","name_org":"Martens, Helle","orcid":"0000-0002-3011-4557","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Connie A.","key":"nicholspau","last":"Nichols","name":"Nichols, Connie A.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Katja S.","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"52088224-13f5-4704-be1e-d37b6bd2f01c","name":"Johansen, Katja S.","orcid":"0000-0002-7587-5990","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"J. Andrew","key":"alspaughpau","last":"Alspaugh","name":"Alspaugh, J. Andrew","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37099613"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.ppat.1010946","issn":["15537366","15537374"],"issn_org":["15537366"],"issue":"4","journal":"PLoS Pathogens","paperid":"e1010946","status":"p","title":"PLoS Pathogens","title_org":"PLOS Pathogens","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85159553278"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d1846565-5596-4085-b0af-b4f4c0c588d8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A fungal lytic polysaccharide monooxygenase is required for cell wall integrity, thermotolerance, and virulence of the fungal human pathogen <i>Cryptococcus neoformans</i>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-671000","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The European hedgehog is in decline, triggering a need to monitor population dynamics to optimise conservation initiatives directed at this species. By counting periosteal growth lines, we determined the age of 388 dead European hedgehogs collected through citizen science in Denmark. The overall mean age was 1.8 years (1.6 years for females and 2.1 years for males), ranging between 0 and 16 years. We constructed life tables showing life expectancies at 2.1 years for females and 2.6 years for males. We discovered that male hedgehogs were more likely to have died in traffic than females, but traffic-related deaths peaked in July for both sexes. A sex difference was detected for non-traffic deaths, as most males died in July, and most females died in September. We created empirical survivorship curves and hazard curves showing that the risk of death for male hedgehogs remains approximately constant with age. In contrast, the risk of death for females increases with age. Most of the collected road-killed individuals died in rural habitats. The degree of inbreeding did not influence longevity. These new insights are important for preparing conservation strategies for the European hedgehog.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Sophie Lund","Berg, Thomas Bjørneboe","Martens, Helle Jakobe","Jones, Owen"],"cuid":["S03-087.50-002507"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Sophie Lund"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oxford"],"keyword":["Age","Age structure","European hedgehogs","Life Tables","Matrix Models","Wildlife conservation","periosteal growth lines","sex biased longevity","sex biased mortality","urban and rural"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Naturama"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anyone can get old all you have to do is live long enough understanding mortality and life expectancy in european hedgehogs erinaceus europaeus","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ani13040626","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research was funded by Beckett-Fonden, grant number 44200; Ingeniør K. A. Rohde og hustrus Legat; Fonden til Værn for Værgeløse Dyr; Iwan Kliem-Larsens Mindelegat; Svalens Fond and Carlsberg Foundation, grant number CF20_0443."],"id":"S03-087.50-002507","identifier":[{"id":"85148879061","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36830413","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9951656","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-3259b103-9430-4390-9cbc-a72b7278e11f","ku-05c7160e-c4b1-4525-bc7a-41aeafe572e8","sdu-e92922bb-013b-4320-8dc9-e4c59c5da538"],"keyword":["European hedgehogs","age","age structure","life tables","matrix models","periosteal growth lines","sex-biased longevity","sex-biased mortality","urban and rural","wildlife conservation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-5B7C621972DBADA12DABCD0DF6BA43CC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/515114226/Rasmussen_et_al._2023._Anyone_Can_Get_Old_All_You_Have_to_Do_Is_Live_Long_Enough_Understanding_Mortality_and_Life_Expectancy_in_European_Hedgehogs_Erinaceus_europaeus_._Animals_2023_13_626.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/341017254/Anyone_Can_Get_Old.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ani13040626","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/222920296/animals_13_00626_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Environmental Biology Monitoring","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section for Bioscience and Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, PopBio"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Naturama"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sophie Lund","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"8d24c1dc-8e08-4781-b6b1-a95629da06b6","name":"Rasmussen, Sophie Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-2975-678X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas B.","key":"bergpau","last":"Berg","locid":"9ba2bdf1-6816-410a-b780-bcdf03e40d40","name":"Berg, Thomas Bjørneboe","name_org":"Berg, Thomas B.","orcid":"0000-0003-0737-1229","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Jakobe","key":"martenspau","last":"Martens","name":"Martens, Helle Jakobe","orcid":"0000-0002-3011-4557","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Owen R.","key":"jonespau","last":"Jones","locid":"d364072a-a2ca-4d06-beda-f6d97306bed9","name":"Jones, Owen","name_org":"Jones, Owen R.","orcid":"0000-0001-5720-4686","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36830413"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/ani13040626","issn":["20762615"],"issue":"4","journal":"Animals","paperid":"626","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute","status":"p","title":"Animals","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85148879061"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3259b103-9430-4390-9cbc-a72b7278e11f","ku-05c7160e-c4b1-4525-bc7a-41aeafe572e8","sdu-e92922bb-013b-4320-8dc9-e4c59c5da538"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Anyone Can Get Old—All You Have to Do Is Live Long Enough : Understanding Mortality and Life Expectancy in European Hedgehogs (Erinaceus europaeus)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-087.50-002507","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Workshop 2 on age reading of North Sea plaice (Pleuronectes platessa), (WKARP2) was the first age reading workshop focusing specifically on age reading of the North Sea plaice stock (ple.27.420) in the North Sea and Skagerrak. The objectives of the workshop were: to evaluate the level of agreement between age readers for the stock by reviewing results of the 2020 North Sea Skagerrak plaice exchange in consideration of previous calibration and validation work; to standardize laboratory procedures and age reading methods applied; to provide guidelines for reliable age interpretation; to provide age error data to the stock assessment working group; to create an agreed age reference collection of otoliths. Two age reading exercises, one exchange before the workshop (SmartDots ID 281), and one workshop exercise (ID 402) were completed using SmartDots1. Age readers’ annotations of growth structures and ageing results from both exercises were examined using standardized quality analyses based on an R script , presented in this report. Age reading error data has been provided to the ICES WGNSSK2 (Working Group on the Assessment of Demersal Stocks in the North Sea and Skagerrak) which can be tested in the ple.27.420 stock assessment model. Disagreement between readers is mostly attributable to differences in the identification of the first winter ring as this can vary in width across samples collected from different areas. Results showed that estimated ages in older fish can be unreliable due to a narrowing of the annuli close to the otolith edge. Further work is required to provide guidelines for age readers about which structures should be identified as annuli. Different preparation methods are applied in national laboratories. The group concluded that reading whole and sectioned otoliths viewed under reflected light is optimal; no obvious benefit was identified from sectioning plaice otoliths from fish under the age of 6. Using images of otoliths, the reliability of the age reading results is depending on image quality. To help standardize image format, lighting and calibration a workshop is recommended to establish a set of guidelines for image quality used in age determination.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Adrian-Schütte, Valeria","Alvestad, Anja Helene","Beier, Ulrika","Bekaert, Karen","Bland, Barbara","Davies, Julie Olivia","de Vries, Marcel","Dussuel, Antoine","Gault, Mandy","Mules, Ruadhan Gillespie","Hansen, Frank Ivan","Hefter-Siebold, Martina","Husebo, Åse","Jennings, Charlotte","Johansson, Jan-Erik","Koelemi, Erika","Krumme, Uwe","Maertens, Ilse","Moerman, Martine","Rasmussen, Helle","Scherffenberg, Louise","Seim, Silje Elisabeth","Smith, Joanne","Telliez, Solène","Wikström, Karolina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-348940"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","France","Germany","Netherlands","Norway","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Centre for the Environment Fisheries and Aquaculture Science","Institut français de recherche pour l'exploitation de la mer","Institute of Marine Research","Johann Heinrich von Thunen Institute","Marine Scotland Science","Research Institute for Agriculture and Fisheries","Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences","Wageningen University & Research"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"workshop 000000000002 on age reading of north sea plaice i pleuronectes platessa i wkarp000000000002 outputs from 000000002021 meeting","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17895/ices.pub.20473083","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-348940","ids":["dtu-94d1c0cf-b119-4aff-bc32-fb114a2972c7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-AC3514D64E0EBBAD38FE8D74F86222E4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/298952763/wkarp2_2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17895/ices.pub.20473083","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"johann heinrich von thunen institute","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Johann Heinrich von Thunen Institute","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"institute of marine research","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Institute of Marine Research","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"wageningen university research","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Wageningen University & Research","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"be","key":"research institute for agriculture and fisheries","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Research Institute for Agriculture and Fisheries","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"se","key":"swedish university of agricultural sciences","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Monitoring and Data"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"fr","key":"institut français de recherche pour l exploitation de la mer","loc":["France","Eu