{"abstract":"Background: Patient head motion is a major concern in clinical brain MRI, as it reduces the diagnostic image quality and may increase examination time and cost. Purpose: To investigate the prevalence of MR images with significant motion artifacts on a given clinical scanner and to estimate the potential financial cost savings of applying motion correction to clinical brain MRI examinations. Study Type: Retrospective. Subjects: In all, 173 patients undergoing a PET/MRI dementia protocol and 55 pediatric patients undergoing a PET/MRI brain tumor protocol. The total scan time of the two protocols were 17 and 40 minutes, respectively. Field Strength/Sequences: 3 T, Siemens mMR Biograph, MPRAGE, DWI, T1 and T2-weighted FLAIR, T2-weighted 2D-FLASH, T2-weighted TSE. Assessment: A retrospective review of image sequences from a given clinical MRI scanner was conducted to investigate the prevalence of motion-corrupted images. The review was performed by three radiologists with different levels of experience using a three-step semiquantitative scale to classify the quality of the images. A total of 1013 sequences distributed on 228 MRI examinations were reviewed. The potential cost savings of motion correction were estimated by a cost estimation for our country with assumptions. Statistical Test: The cost estimation was conducted with a 20% lower and upper bound on the model assumptions to include the uncertainty of the assumptions. Results: 7.9% of the sequences had motion artifacts that decreased the interpretability, while 2.0% of the sequences had motion artifacts causing the images to be nondiagnostic. The estimated annual cost to the clinic/hospital due to patient head motion per scanner was $45,066 without pediatric examinations and $364,242 with pediatric examinations. Data Conclusion: The prevalence of a motion-corrupted image was found in 2.0% of the reviewed sequences. Based on the model, repayment periods are presented as a function of the price for applying motion correction and its performance. Evidence Level: 4. Technical Efficacy: Stage 6 J. Magn. Reson. Imaging 2020;52:731–738.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Slipsager, Jakob Mølkjær","Glimberg, Stefan L.","Søgaard, Jes","Paulsen, Rasmus Reinhold","Johannesen, Helle H.","Martens, Pernille C.","Seth, Alka","Marner, Lisbeth","Henriksen, Otto M.","Olesen, Oline Vinter","Højgaard, Liselotte"],"cuid":["S03-099.64-032626"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Slipsager, Jakob M.","Slipsager, Jakob Mølkjær"],"keyword":["Cost saving","MRI","Motion artifacts","Motion correction","Neuroimaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quantifying the financial savings of motion correction in brain mri a model based estimate of the costs arising from patient head motion and potential savings from implementation of motion correction","src":["dtu","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/290407910/Quantifying_the_Financial_Savings_of_Motion_Correction_in_Brain_MRI_accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Contract grant sponsor: John and Birthe Meyer Foundation The Danish Childhood Cancer Foundation."],"id":"S03-099.64-032626","identifier":[{"id":"32144848","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85081385317","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-029855cd-f7ac-4cfa-83c8-c42d60898650","ku-27b9201a-d4e2-4e51-a7cc-25724c536a80","sdu-92626879-cb59-442b-a67c-778c1d149df9"],"keyword":["Cost saving","MRI","Motion artifacts","Motion correction","Neuroimaging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-8CBF228704745E0D35CD5657AB6B4233"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/254094394/jmri.27112.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170405842/jmri.27112.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/290407910/Quantifying_the_Financial_Savings_of_Motion_Correction_in_Brain_MRI_accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Visual Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["TracInnovations"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Psychiatry (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4