{"abstract":"A novel bacterial strain, S40T, with strong antifungal activity was isolated from the rhizosphere of green potato collected from Zealand, Denmark. Polyphasic analysis with a combined phenotypic, phylogenetic and genomic approach was used to characterize S40T. Phylogenetic analysis based on the 16S rRNA gene and MLSA (concatenated gyrB, rpoD, infB and atpD sequences) showed that strain S40T was affiliated with the genus Serratia and with Serratia plymuthica PRI-2C as the closest related strain [average nucleotide identity (ANI), 99.26%; DNA–DNA hybridization (dDDH), 99.20%]. However, whole genome sequence analyses revealed that S40T and S. plymuthica PRI-2C genomes displayed lower similarities when compared to all other S. plymuthica strains (ANI ≤94.34%; dDDH ≤57.6% relatedness). The DNA G+C content of strain S40T was determined to be 55.9 mol%. Cells of the strain were Gram-negative, rod-shaped, facultative anaerobic and displayed growth at 10–37 °C (optimum, 25–30 °C) and at pH 6–9 (optimum, pH 6–7). Major fatty acids were C16:0 (27.9%), summed feature (C16:1 ω6c/C16:1 ω7c; 18.0%) and C17:0 cyclo (15.1%). The respiratory quinone was determined to be Q8 (94%) and MK8 (95%) and the major polar lipids were phosphatidylethanolamine and phosphatidylglycerol. The results of phenotypic, phylogenetic and genomic analyses support the hypothesis that strain S40T represents a novel species of the genus Serratia, for which the name Serratia inhibens sp. nov. is proposed. The type strain is S40T (=LMG 31467T=NCIMB 15235T). In addition, we propose that S. plymuthica PRI-2C is reclassified and transferred to the species S. inhibens as S. inhibens PRI-2C.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hennessy, Rosanna C.","Dichmann, Søs I.","Martens, Helle Juel","Zervas, Athanasios","Stougaard, Peter"],"cuid":["S02-099.93-013755"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Stougaard, Peter"],"keyword":["Antimicrobial activity","Potato","Serratia","Whole genome analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"i serratia inhibens i sp nov a new antifungal species isolated from potato i solanum tuberosum i","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/286843503/4204_ijsem004270.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.93-013755","identifier":[{"id":"32553053","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85088880378","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000560646100019","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-10180d33-1190-4940-8846-8ab25a64a539","ku-e9e617e2-a6cd-4ffe-9895-7d447fcc4046"],"keyword":["ANI","Antimicrobial activity","DDDH","Potato","Serratia","Whole genome analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CB7F210C3BCFC46723944467F9E4340F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/286843503/4204_ijsem004270.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Microbial Ecology and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Environmental Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Rosanna Catherine","key":"hennessypau","last":"Hennessy","locid":"04bc8ab2-b475-47c6-9a47-c7d1394344b3","name":"Hennessy, Rosanna Catherine","orcid":"0000-0002-2359-8565","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Søs Inger","key":"dichmannpau","last":"Dichmann","name":"Dichmann, Søs Inger","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helle Juel","key":"martenspau","last":"Martens","locid":"cd7f808e-0b4a-4423-9846-d3a81d0fad26","name":"Martens, Helle Juel","orcid":"0000-0002-3011-4557","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Athanasios","key":"zervaspau","last":"Zervas","locid":"5cc56a8f-ee51-4e5c-97c6-225dd8421bdc","name":"Zervas, Athanasios","orcid":"0000-0002-4706-4023","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"stougaardpau","last":"Stougaard","locid":"777a39fb-80d5-4edb-aae2-6f8e7707404d","name":"Stougaard, Peter","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32553053"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1099/ijsem.0.004270","issn":["10706259","14665026"],"issn_org":["14665026"],"issue":"7","journal":"International Journal of Systematic and Evolutionary Microbiology","pages":"4204-4211","paperid":"004270","publisher":"Microbiology Society","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Systematic and Evolutionary Microbiology","volume":"70"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088880378"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-10180d33-1190-4940-8846-8ab25a64a539","ku-e9e617e2-a6cd-4ffe-9895-7d447fcc4046"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"<i>Serratia inhibens </i>sp. nov., a new antifungal species isolated from potato (<i>Solanum tuberosum</i>)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.93-013755","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The plant hormone auxin serves as central regulator of growth and development. Auxin transporters in the plasma membrane are assumed to define tissue-level patterns of auxin distribution [1, 2]. However, auxin is small enough to diffuse through the plasmodesmata that connect neighboring cells [3], presenting an alternative pathway, whose contribution to auxin transport remained largely unexplored [4]. Here, photoactivation microscopy [5, 6] was used to measure the capacity for small-molecule diffusion in the epidermis of Arabidopsis thaliana leaves. In the elongated epidermis cells covering the midrib and petiole, the plasmodesmata-mediated cell-wall permeability was found to be several times higher in the longitudinal than in the transverse direction. The physiological relevance of this asymmetry was tested through quantification of the shade-avoidance response, which depends on auxin transport from the leaf tip to the petiole in the abaxial side of the leaf [7], with the hypothesis that directionality of diffusion supplements transporter-mediated auxin movement [8]. Triggering the response by auxin application at the tip led to stronger leaf movement in wild-type plants than in gsl8 mutants [9], which lack the callose synthase necessary to establish directionality. The results match the predictions of a mathematical model of auxin transport based on the permeabilities measured in wild-type and mutant plants. It is concluded that plasmodesmata permeability can be selectively modulated within a plant cell and that the conferred directionality in diffusion can influence the tissue-specific distribution patterns of small molecules, like auxin.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Gao, Chen","Liu, Xiangdong","De Storme, Nico","Jensen, Kaare Hartvig","Xu, Qiyu","Yang, Jintao","Liu, Xiaohui","Chen, Shaolin","Martens, Helle Juel","Schulz, Alexander","Liesche, Johannes"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-035788"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KU Leuven","Northwest Normal University","South China Agricultural University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"directionality of plasmodesmata mediated transport in arabidopsis leaves supports auxin channeling","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2020.03.014","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-035788","identifier":[{"id":"000534622700059","type":"wos"},{"id":"85084589518","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32275878","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-8b018fab-2695-4c61-8e07-7baf266baf02","ku-3b14c9a1-f27c-4c2b-81b7-fcdc7f53a5bb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CA4E25A2C7298F5643A77BA903BE3142"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/286622180/1_s2.0_S0960982220303523_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2020.03.014","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/256223464/1_s2.0_S0960982220303523_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"northwest normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northwest Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"south china agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"South China Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"be","key":"ku leuven","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"KU Leuven","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Biophysics and Fluids"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Transport Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chen","key":"gaochenpau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Chen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiangdong","key":"liuxiangdongpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Xiangdong","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nico","key":"destormenicopau","last":"De Storme","name":"De Storme, Nico","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kaare Hartvig","key":"jensenkaarehartvigpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"c5e52e6d-6152-4d19-9e38-f344cc56a318","name":"Jensen, Kaare Hartvig","orcid":"0000-0003-0787-5283","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qiyu","key":"xuqiyupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Qiyu","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jintao","key":"yangjintaopau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Jintao","rank":6,"