817804166592"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Identification of an algal xylan synthase indicates that there is functional orthology between algal and plant cell wall biosynthesis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-430110","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"β-Glucan dietary fiber rich food systems hold a great potential for improving human health. Here, we evaluate the extractability and quality of β-glucan liquid formulations from eight different barley genotypes varying in β-glucan content and molecular structure using Termamyl® SC (T), Attenuzyme® (A) and Attenuzyme® Flex (AF) amylolytic enzymes in combinations. Extracts from barley lines Lys5f, KVL408, KVL1104 and CDC Fibar exceeded 4 g β-glucan/l, providing European Food Safety Authority (EFSA) and U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) recommended amounts (3 g β-glucan/day) from three portions. TAF extracts of Lys5f and KVL408 grains reached extraordinary high concentrations of 8–9 g β-glucan/l. The β-glucan molecular mass decreased with enzyme treatment T < TA < TAF due to minor lichenase side activity. Extractability was generally higher and molecular mass lower for barley lines low in triosyl/tetraosyl (DP3/DP4) ratios than for those high in DP3/DP4 ratios (Lys5f, KVL408 and KVL1104). Overall, the higher β-glucan content and structural robustness in Lys5f and KVL408 raw materials favor these in a β-glucan rich extract with potential for EFSA and FDA health and nutrition claims.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Mikkelsen, Mette S.","Meier, Sebastian","Jensen, Morten G.","Qin, Fen","Stoica, Iuliana-Madalina","Martens, Helle J.","Blennow, Andreas","Jespersen, Birthe M."],"cuid":["S02-098.76-037173"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Barley beta glucans","Enzymatic hydrolysis","Extractability","Molecular Structure"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CARL"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CARL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"barley genotypic β glucan variation combined with enzymatic modifications direct its potential as a natural ingredient in a high fiber extract","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/201862011/Barley_genotypic_glucan_variation_2017_accepted.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-098.76-037173","identifier":[{"id":"85016141146","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-cb4b5473-0ba0-4846-8193-a6afe1822476","ku-2b1e7122-0f27-427a-9e11-40a43a07bb60"],"keyword":["Barley beta-glucans","Enzymatic hydrolysis","Extractability","Molecular structure"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D15BD06EF56D8F8535238C2251C29294"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/201862011/Barley_genotypic_glucan_variation_2017_accepted.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/128951202/1_s2.0_S0733521016303277_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Ingredient and Dairy Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry","Technical Unive