of Cereal Science","pages":"45-53","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cereal Science","volume":"75"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85016141146"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-cb4b5473-0ba0-4846-8193-a6afe1822476","ku-2b1e7122-0f27-427a-9e11-40a43a07bb60"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Barley genotypic β-glucan variation combined with enzymatic modifications direct its potential as a natural ingredient in a high fiber extract","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.76-037173","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Ravn, Jonas Laukkonen","Martens, Helle Juel","Pettersson, Dan","Pedersen, Ninfa Rangel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-538303"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a commercial gh000000000011 xylanase mediates xylan solubilisation and degradation in wheat rye and barley as demonstrated by microscopy techniques and wet chemistry methods","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-538303","identifier":[{"id":"84990946299","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f2b82cf9-eb16-4d5f-ac79-d750f19c005a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CB26FC8403CD1BDC3D7D3F3D481E609E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"novonesis","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOSI","l3nn":"Novonesis","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novonesis","namevar":["Novozymes"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOSI","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Transport Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas Laukkonen","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","name":"Ravn, Jonas Laukkonen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Helle Juel","key":"martenspau","last":"Martens","locid":"cd7f808e-0b4a-4423-9846-d3a81d0fad26","name":"Martens, Helle Juel","orcid":"0000-0002-3011-4557","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dan","key":"petterssonpau","last":"Pettersson","name":"Pettersson, Dan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ninfa Rangel","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Ninfa Rangel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.anifeedsci.2016.06.020","issn":["03778401","18732216"],"issn_org":["03778401"],"journal":"Animal Feed Science and Technology","pages":"216-225","status":"p","title":"Animal Feed Science and Technology","volume":"219"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84990946299"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f2b82cf9-eb16-4d5f-ac79-d750f19c005a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A commercial GH11 xylanase mediates xylan solubilisation and degradation in wheat, rye and barley as demonstrated by microscopy techniques and wet chemistry methods","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-538303","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Plant chloroplasts are light-driven cell factories that have great potential to act as a chassis for metabolic engineering applications. Using plant chloroplasts, we demonstrate how photosynthetic reducing power can drive a metabolic pathway to synthesise a bio-active natural product. For this purpose, we stably engineered the dhurrin pathway from Sorghum bicolor into the chloroplasts of Nicotiana tabacum (tobacco). Dhurrin is a cyanogenic glucoside and its synthesis from the amino acid tyrosine is catalysed by two membrane-bound cytochrome P450 enzymes (CYP79A1 and CYP71E1) and a soluble glucosyltransferase (UGT85B1), and is dependent on electron transfer from a P450 oxidoreductase. The entire pathway was introduced into the chloroplast by integrating CYP79A1, CYP71E1, and UGT85B1 into a neutral site of the N. tabacum chloroplast genome. The two P450s and the UGT85B1 were functional when expressed in the chloroplasts and converted endogenous tyrosine into dhurrin using electrons derived directly from the photosynthetic electron transport chain, without the need for the presence of an NADPH-dependent P450 oxidoreductase. The dhurrin produced in the engineered plants amounted to 0.1-0.2% of leaf dry weight compared to 6% in sorghum. The results obtained pave the way for plant P450s involved in the synthesis of economically important compounds to be engineered into the thylakoid membrane of chloroplasts, and demonstrate that their full catalytic cycle can be driven directly by photosynthesis-derived electrons.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Gnanasekaran, Thiyagarajan","Karcher, Daniel","Nielsen, Agnieszka Janina Zygadlo","Martens, Helle Juel","Ruf, Stephanie","Kroop, Xenia","Olsen, Carl Erik","Motawie, Mohammed Saddik","Pribil, Mathias","Møller, Birger Lindberg","Bock, Ralph","Jensen, Poul Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-521262"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article","Research Support Non U S Gov t"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transfer of the cytochrome p000000000450 dependent dhurrin pathway from i sorghum bicolor i into i nicotiana tabacum i chloroplasts for light driven synthesis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/jxb/erw067","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-521262","identifier":[{"id":"26969746","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84963930543","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4809297","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-d5f31b74-e8fc-4b10-afe9-fecc9f51e8e2"],"keyword":["Journal Article","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E9B1A6856E006BD284A74013BA2F7497"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/jxb/erw067","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/169883863/J._Exp._Bot._2016_Gnanasekaran_2495_506.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Molecular Plant Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Thiyagarajan","key":"gnanasekaranpau","last":"Gnanasekaran","locid":"980370f3-1c86-4c90-8fc9-3d483f9714e0","name":"Gnanasekaran, Thiyagarajan","orcid":"0000-0001-8645-7703","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniel","key":"karcherpau","last":"Karcher","name":"Karcher, Daniel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Agnieszka Janina Zygadlo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d46153ce-157c-41de-9fc5-d00bf0613718","name":"Nielsen, Agnieszka Janina Zygadlo","orcid":"0000-0002-7948-8912","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Helle Juel","key":"martenspau","last":"Martens","locid":"cd7f808e-0b4a-4423-9846-d3a81d0fad26","name":"Martens, Helle Juel","orcid":"0000-0002-3011-4557","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Stephanie","key":"rufpau","last":"Ruf","name":"Ruf, Stephanie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xenia","key":"krooppau","last":"Kroop","name":"Kroop, Xenia","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carl Erik","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"abcd3923-e43e-4a0e-b104-4b6238e5afc8","name":"Olsen, Carl Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-2275-0596","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mohammed Saddik","key":"motawiepau","last":"Motawie","locid":"4fb3ebbf-108e-4e10-a770-d99815eb6372","name":"Motawie, Mohammed Saddik","orcid":"0000-0001-5582-9463","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mathias","key":"pribilpau","last":"Pribil","locid":"755dd902-1537-4279-8630-7098d49ce6ee","name":"Pribil, Mathias","orcid":"0000-0002-9174-9548","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Birger Lindberg","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"54d5ec55-f24e-4492-9e76-2c5478d312e0","name":"Møller, Birger Lindberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3252-3119","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ralph","key":"bockpau","last":"Bock","name":"Bock, Ralph","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Poul Erik","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"cb8fdf4a-6052-43b4-b731-384346885e4d","name":"Jensen, Poul Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-6524-7723","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26969746"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/jxb/erw067","issn":["00220957","14602431"],"issn_org":["00220957"],"issue":"8","journal":"Journal of Experimental Botany","pages":"2495-2506","status":"p","title":"Journal of Experimental Botany","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84963930543"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d5f31b74-e8fc-4b10-afe9-fecc9f51e8e2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Transfer of the cytochrome P450-dependent dhurrin pathway from <i>Sorghum bicolor</i> into <i>Nicotiana tabacum</i> chloroplasts for light-driven synthesis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-521262","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Metabolic highways may be orchestrated by the assembly of sequential enzymes into protein complexes, or metabolons, to facilitate efficient channeling of intermediates and to prevent undesired metabolic cross-talk while maintaining metabolic flexibility. Here we report the isolation of the dynamic metabolon that catalyzes the formation of the cyanogenic glucoside dhurrin, a defense compound produced in sorghum plants. The metabolon was reconstituted in liposomes, which demonstrated the importance of membrane surface charge and the presence of the glucosyltransferase for metabolic channeling. We used in planta fluorescence lifetime imaging microscopy and fluorescence correlation spectroscopy to study functional and structural characteristics of the metabolon. Understanding the regulation of biosynthetic metabolons offers opportunities to optimize synthetic biology approaches for efficient production of high-value products in heterologous hosts.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Laursen, Tomas","Borch-Jensen, Jonas","Knudsen, Camilla","Bavishi, Krutika","Torta, Federico","Martens, Helle Juel","Silvestro, Daniele","Hatzakis, Nikos S.","Wenk, Markus R","Dafforn, Timothy R","Olsen, Carl Erik","Motawie, Mohammed Saddik","Hamberger, Björn Robert","Møller, Birger Lindberg","Bassard, Jean-Étienne André"],"cuid":["S02-089.54-040774"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, South","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Singapore","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Her Majesty's Government","Joint BioEnergy Institute","National University of Singapore","University of Birmingham"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterization of a dynamic metabolon producing the defense compound dhurrin in sorghum","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84995900407","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-089.54-040774","identifier":[{"id":"84995900407","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27856908","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-20be4fac-793c-4d29-83b0-af0b409234ff","sdu-b46f8437-3032-48b2-9f25-855b6e064349"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B5D36649892878F866631DF5004A0DD2"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Plant Biochemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Biosynergy A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"sg","key":"national university of singapore","loc":["Singapore","Asia, 